								<a class="accordion-button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
									Q: 1. What is UAE attestation and why is it required?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> UAE attestation is the process of verifying and authenticating documents for use in the United Arab Emirates. UAE attestation is required to ensure the authenticity and legitimacy of documents for personal, educational, professional and commercial purposes in the UAE.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
									Q: 2. What types of documents can be attested for UAE?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> Various documents, including birth certificates, marriage certificates, educational certificates, and commercial documents, can be attested for UAE.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
									Q: 3. What is basic requirement for documents to be attested?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> Documents should be in their original form, with all required signatures, stamps, and seals. Laminated documents are not accepted. The pre-attestation process which may involve authentication by Notary, Ministry of External Affairs, Sub Divisional Magistrate, Ministry of Human Resource & Development, Chambers of Commerce, Ministry of Justice (all /some of these based on the nature of the document) should be complete before documents are submitted with the Hon’ble Mission for attestation.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree1">
									Q: 4. What is the process to register for UAE Attestation?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> Please visit MOFA UAE website <a href="https://www.mofa.gov.ae/en" target="_blank">https://www.mofa.gov.ae/en</a>. You would require to download UAE Pass App and register with your valid ID and create a Login ID. Visit the ‘Services’ tab and select ‘Document Attestation’ and choose ‘UAE Embassy & Consulate Abroad’. Post this, please register the document on website and make payment online on website. You have to print receipt and submit along with the original copy of attached document. </p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree2">
									Q: 5. What is Document fees charged by the Ministry?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> Fee for attesting a personal document by Consulate/ Embassy is AED 150 per document. Fee for attesting a Commercial document by Consulate/Embassy is AED 2000 per document. All this would be paid online or local currency (only in Russia) on the above mentioned link of MOFA UAE.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree3">
									Q: 6. What is BLS Delivery Services?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> The BLS Delivery Services allows applicants for collection, submission and dispatch of documents for a service fee. BLS Service fee is AED 15 per document( maximum 25 documents are accepted in an application) in Mumbai, Spain. </p>
									<p>BLS Service fee is AED 129 per application (with maximum of 5 documents) in Russia. This fee would be paid online only on the above mentioned link of MOFA UAE along with Document Attestation Charges levied by the esteemed Ministry. In Russia, the applicants can pay fee in local currency at BLS Office.</p>
									<ul class="list">
										<li><strong>Get in Touch by Call or Email:</strong> Reach out to our specialists with your questions, and they will guide you with all the required details.</li>
										<li><strong>Provide your address for collection:</strong> Let us know where to collect your documents from, or if you prefer, you can drop them off at our location. </li>
										<li><strong>Process Initiation and Confirmation:</strong> After we confirm your details, our team will start the attestation process.</li>
										<li><strong>Document Submission to the Mission and Return:</strong> We'll guide you through the procedure, submit your documents with Mission on your behalf and ensure your documents are returned to you promptly</li>
									</ul>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree4">
									Q: 7. How long does the UAE attestation process take?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> The processing time varies depending on the type of document. Usually document attestation may take 24-48 hrs post submission with the Mission in Mumbai Spain and 3-5 working days in Russia.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree5">
									Q: 8. Can I track the status of my attestation application?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> A unique ATS reference number is generated for every registered application. You can use this ATS reference number to track the status of your application through our <a href="index.php">website</a>, <a href="mailto:attestation-uae@blsinternational.com">attestation-uae@blsinternational.com</a> or by contacting our Customer Support Team to know the status of your application. At the same time, we facilitate you with email notification while your application is delivered to the Mission for attestation as well as once it is ready for collection/ dispatch.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree6">
									Q: 9. Is my personal and document information secure?
								</a>
							</div>
							<div id="collapseThree6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
								<div class="accordion-body">
									<p><strong>Ans: </strong> Yes, we ensure the confidentiality and security of your information through our robust data protection policies and encryption technologies. We also take full diligence in systematic collection and delivery of documents.</p>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="accordion-item">
							<div class="accordion-header">
								<a class="accordion-button collapsed" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree7">
									Q: 10. Do I need to be physically present myself for UAE attestation?
